# Code owners — the human backstop for the Constitution rules no tool enforces.
#
# `docs/PARITY-MATRIX.md` lists which rules are machine-enforced. Rule #4 ("never invent a
# selector, URL, endpoint, or UI string") is irreducibly unmechanizable — it is about process, not
# syntax — so review is the ONLY gate on it. These paths are where breaking it does the most
# damage, because a wrong value there is copied into every test written afterwards.
#
# ⚠️ REPLACE @sayurionishi with your own team handle when you adopt this scaffold.

# Default owner for everything.
*                       @sayurionishi

# The AI rule layer. A change here changes what every agent generates from now on, for both Claude
# and Copilot, so it deserves a second pair of eyes more than most code does.
/rules/                  @sayurionishi
/CLAUDE.md               @sayurionishi
/AGENTS.md               @sayurionishi
/.claude/                @sayurionishi
/.github/copilot-instructions.md  @sayurionishi
/.github/instructions/   @sayurionishi
/docs/PARITY-MATRIX.md   @sayurionishi

# Enforcement itself. Loosening a rule here silently loosens it everywhere.
/eslint.config.mjs       @sayurionishi
/scripts/constitution-guard.ts    @sayurionishi

# Single sources of truth. A wrong value here is invisible and propagates (rule #4, #11).
/config/                 @sayurionishi
/enums/                  @sayurionishi
